WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.712
The school expects a diagnostic-quality twelve-lead in under three minutes from contact in a cooperative, appropriate patient. This is a specific training target, not permission to omit resuscitation, consent or correct placement.
学校要求对适合且合作的患者，从接触起三分钟内取得诊断质量12导联。这是训练目标，不允许省略复苏、同意或正确定位。

00:00:14.712 --> 00:00:28.152
Module Seven G also introduces STEMI patterns, equivalents and mimics. We teach the recognition concepts while keeping current operational authorization separate from a classroom interpretation exercise.
7G还介绍STEMI图形、等同表现及模仿情况。我们教授识别概念，但将当前运行授权与课堂判图练习分开。

00:00:28.152 --> 00:00:39.648
A lead map suggests anatomical views; it does not prove a culprit artery or the absence of dangerous disease. The patient and evolving findings remain central.
导联图提示解剖视角，不能证明责任血管，也不能排除危险疾病。患者及演变所见始终是中心。

00:00:39.648 --> 00:00:49.128
The source notes distinguish the saved school wording from current public BCEHS workflow. Do not combine the two into a new invented treatment rule.
来源说明区分学校存档措辞与当前公开BCEHS流程。不能把二者混成自创治疗规则。

00:00:49.128 --> 00:01:01.008
An electrode is a physical contact. A lead is a calculated view of electrical activity. Four limb contacts and six chest contacts create the standard twelve-lead information.
电极是实体接触点，导联是计算出的电活动视角。四个肢体和六个胸部接触点，产生标准十二导联信息。

00:01:01.008 --> 00:01:11.352
The six limb views look in the frontal plane, while the precordial views sample the horizontal plane. A monitoring strip supplies less spatial information.
六个肢体导联观察额状面，胸前导联观察水平面。单条监护记录提供的空间信息较少。

00:01:11.352 --> 00:01:21.480
This is not twelve different heartbeats or twelve physical sensors. The displayed arrangement may vary, so read the actual lead labels and recording format.
这不是十二次不同心搏，也不是十二个实体传感器。显示排列可能不同，应读真实导联名称及记录格式。

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:32.592
Multiple views help recognize regional changes, but correct geometry and signal quality are necessary. A wrong position can create a plausible but misleading picture.
多视角有助识别区域变化，但需正确位置和信号质量。位置错误可产生看似合理却误导的图形。

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:42.528
Explain that you need skin contacts on the limbs and chest to record the heart's electrical activity. Describe the exposure and what the patient will feel.
解释需要在肢体及胸部贴电极，记录心脏电活动；还应说明需暴露哪些部位，以及患者会有什么感受。

00:01:42.528 --> 00:01:56.496
Obtain appropriate consent and address questions or preferences. An emergency incapacity situation uses the actual legal process, not a routine assumption that every chest-pain patient has implicitly agreed.
应取得适当同意，回应问题及偏好。急症无决策能力时须走真实法律流程，不能假定所有胸痛者都已默许。

00:01:56.496 --> 00:02:08.832
Use draping and respectful assistance, particularly when chest landmarks lie under breast tissue. Do not substitute exposed nipple position for a true anatomical landmark.
应遮盖并提供尊重的协助，尤其定位在乳房组织下时。不能把外露乳头位置当作真实解剖标志。

00:02:08.832 --> 00:02:20.736
Use a tolerable supine or semi-recumbent position as appropriate and support limbs. Do not force a breathless patient flat or ask a failing patient to perform a prolonged breath-hold.
适当时采用可耐受平卧或半卧，并支撑肢体。不能强迫气促者平躺，也不能要求正在衰竭者长时间屏气。

00:02:20.736 --> 00:02:33.192
Colour mnemonics depend on the cable standard. Check the printed RA, LA, RL and LL labels and the actual trained monitor procedure instead of assuming one colour sequence worldwide.
颜色口诀取决于线缆标准。应核印刷RA、LA、RL、LL标签及实际受训仪器方法，不能假定全球颜色顺序相同。

00:02:33.192 --> 00:02:45.264
Use approved limb sites with good contact and avoid placing electrodes directly over bone. Keep comparable left/right placement and support the limbs to reduce muscle noise.
采用获准且接触良好的肢体位置，避免直接贴在骨面。左右位置应可比较，并支撑肢体减少肌肉噪声。

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:57.216
Do not casually move diagnostic limb electrodes to the torso just to make the trace look cleaner. Modified placement can change waveforms and needs its actual protocol and notation.
不能只为图形干净，就随意把诊断肢体电极移到躯干。改位可改变波形，需要真实规程及标注。

00:02:57.216 --> 00:03:09.864
If body habitus, injury or access requires deviation, obtain appropriate guidance and record the actual sites and position so serial comparisons are not falsely reassuring.
体型、损伤或可接近性要求偏离时，应取得指导，并记录真实位置和体位，避免连续比较造成错误安心。

00:03:09.864 --> 00:03:20.808
The sternal angle helps identify the second rib. Count intercostal spaces downward to the fourth space rather than estimating by eye or by the nipple.
胸骨角有助识别第二肋，再向下数到第四肋间。不能凭目测或乳头估计。

00:03:20.808 --> 00:03:29.544
V one is at the right sternal border in the fourth intercostal space, and V two is at the left sternal border in the fourth space.
V1在右胸骨缘第四肋间，V2在左胸骨缘第四肋间。

00:03:29.544 --> 00:03:40.296
Putting V one and V two too high is a common avoidable source of misleading changes. Confirm the landmark before interpreting an unexpected anterior pattern.
V1、V2放太高是常见且可避免的误导来源。判读意外前壁变化前，应先确认定位。

00:03:40.296 --> 00:03:52.176
Practice landmarking on the school model with feedback. A flat diagram can show relationships but cannot substitute for supervised palpation on different body shapes.
应在学校模型上练定位并接受反馈。平面图只能显示关系，不能替代对不同体型的督导触诊。

00:03:52.176 --> 00:04:01.968
Find V four at the fifth intercostal space on the mid-clavicular line. Then place V three between the already located V two and V four.
先在锁骨中线第五肋间找V4，再把V3放在已定位的V2和V4之间。

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:13.512
Place V five at the anterior axillary line and V six at the mid-axillary line in the same horizontal plane as V four. Do not follow a descending rib curve around the chest.
V5在腋前线，V6在腋中线，二者与V4保持同一水平。不能沿向下弯的肋骨曲线绕胸放置。

00:04:13.512 --> 00:04:26.472
Check the contact and actual positions before acquisition. Breast tissue, adiposity, dressings and clothing should prompt respectful correct access, not a guess at an approximate spot.
采集前核实际位置及接触。乳房、脂肪、敷料或衣物应促使尊重且正确地接近部位，而不是随便估位置。

00:04:26.472 --> 00:04:35.976
The diagram is relational, not a scale body map. State the landmarks aloud and ask an instructor to verify placement during practice.
图示表达关系，不是按比例的人体地图。应说出标志，并在练习中请教师核定位。

00:04:35.976 --> 00:04:48.048
The correct chest-wall location may be under breast tissue. Explain and provide privacy and appropriate assistance rather than placing a sensor over an arbitrary more convenient area.
正确胸壁位置可能在乳房组织下。应解释、保护隐私并提供适当协助，不能随意贴在更方便的地方。

00:04:48.048 --> 00:04:57.768
Larger or smaller body size does not replace anatomical landmarking with a fixed number of centimetres from a nipple. Palpate what you need to identify.
身体大小不能取代解剖定位，也不能改为距乳头固定厘米数。应触认真正需要的结构。

00:04:57.768 --> 00:05:11.184
When injuries, dressings or skin condition prevent usual placement, use the actual trained alternative and communicate the modification. Do not interpret a modified trace as if nothing changed.
损伤、敷料或皮肤情况阻碍常规定位时，应采用真实受训替代并交代改动。不能把改位记录当作什么都没变。

00:05:11.184 --> 00:05:22.680
For repeat ECGs, comparable placement and posture make change more interpretable. Record important unavoidable differences with the time and symptoms.
复查时位置及姿势可比较，变化才更容易解释。重要且无法避免的差异，应与时间及症状一并记录。

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:34.224
Before the encounter, organize the actual equipment and check consumables. An untangled cable and sound electrodes save time without cutting patient safeguards.
接触患者前先整理真实器材并查耗材。理顺线缆、确保电极完好，可以节约时间而不牺牲安全。

00:05:34.224 --> 00:05:44.688
Prepare the skin using the approved technique, accounting for moisture, hair and sensitivity. Do not apply an improvised abrasive or chemical method.
按获准方法准备皮肤，考虑潮湿、毛发和敏感。不能临时发明磨擦或化学处理。

00:05:44.688 --> 00:05:55.440
Check connections and relieve traction. When ready, calmly ask the patient to rest the limbs, avoid talking and breathe normally for the short acquisition.
核连接并减牵拉。准备好后平静请患者放松肢体、短暂不说话并正常呼吸。

00:05:55.440 --> 00:06:07.752
When acquisition fails, troubleshoot a specific cause instead of repeatedly pressing print. Continue assessment and avoid turning an equipment problem into a prolonged scene delay.
采集失败时应针对原因排查，不能反复只按打印。要继续评患者，避免器材问题变成长时间现场延误。

00:06:07.752 --> 00:06:17.520
Verify that all twelve views are present and labelled, with readable complexes and a usable baseline. Check speed and gain before measuring.
核十二个视角齐全且有标签，波群可读、基线可用。测量前先查速度和增益。

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:27.336
Enter accurate identity and device-required demographic data. Wrong patient details can misdirect a transmission or influence automated processing.
应准确输入身份及仪器要求的人口学资料。资料错误可能误发记录，也可能影响自动处理。

00:06:27.336 --> 00:06:39.696
Record when symptoms and acquisition occurred and what care was given. Select the correct ECG record for transmission; sending a previous person's tracing is not a minor labelling issue.
记录症状、采集及照护时间，传输时选择正确记录。把前一人的图发出去，不是小标签问题。

00:06:39.696 --> 00:06:50.040
Check the actual transmission result and communicate failure through the appropriate alternative. A send button alone does not prove the receiving team has the tracing.
要检查实际传输结果，失败时按适当替代方式沟通。按发送键不证明接收团队已拿到记录。

00:06:50.040 --> 00:07:02.952
Start the practice clock at patient contact, as the school specifies for a cooperative appropriate patient. Assign a primary assessor and an acquisition partner so necessary tasks run in parallel.
按学校要求，对合作且适合患者从接触开始计时。分主评估者和采集同伴，让必要工作并行。

00:07:02.952 --> 00:07:16.872
Use the first practice to locate the bottleneck: equipment preparation, exposure/consent, landmarking, data entry or troubleshooting. Improve that step rather than sacrificing accuracy.
首次练习应找瓶颈：器材、暴露同意、定位、资料输入或故障排查。应改善该环节，不是牺牲准确性。

00:07:16.872 --> 00:07:27.984
Stop the clock only when the required tracing is actually acquired and readable, not when the last electrode is attached. Record actual time and any quality failure.
只有真正采到所需且可读记录才停表，不是贴完最后电极就算。要记录真实时间及质量失败。

00:07:27.984 --> 00:07:40.080
If urgent breathing or circulation support takes priority, state that and provide it. Do not meet a classroom target by delaying a more important intervention or falsely documenting a time.
紧急呼吸或循环支持更优先时，应说明并实施。不能为达课堂目标，延误重要干预或虚记时间。

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:51.888
The current handbook has separate LifePak Fifteen and ZOLL acquisition pages. Buttons, demographics, noise handling and transmission workflow are not interchangeable.
当前手册分别列LifePak 15和ZOLL采集页。按键、人口学输入、噪声及传输流程不能互换。

00:07:51.888 --> 00:08:02.952
The school exercise must be practised on its actual monitor. This lecture supplies the reasoning and sequence, not a claim that a generic diagram trains every device.
学校练习必须在真实监护仪上完成。本课提供推理及顺序，不能声称一张通用图就训练了所有器材。

00:08:02.952 --> 00:08:11.688
Do not invent an override when noisy data prevents a recording. Follow the device-specific authorization and obtain appropriate help.
噪声阻碍采集时，不能自创覆盖操作。应遵具体器材授权，并寻求适当协助。

00:08:11.688 --> 00:08:24.168
The current PCP workflow warns to leave the twelve-lead acquisition screen when not actively acquiring because ongoing rhythm detection can be affected. Confirm the actual monitoring mode after recording.
当前PCP流程提醒：非正在采集时应离开12导联采集屏，因为持续节律检测可能受影响。记录后要确认真实监护模式。

00:08:24.168 --> 00:08:33.672
An early ECG can be nondiagnostic while disease evolves. Save the initial record and link it to the symptom state and relevant treatment.
病变演变中，早期心电可能无诊断性。应保存初始记录，并关联当时症状及相关治疗。

00:08:33.672 --> 00:08:44.256
Repeat according to the actual pathway and clinical change. Deterioration requires immediate reassessment, not waiting for a scheduled ten-minute recording.
按真实路径和临床变化复查。恶化需要立即重评，不能等预定十分钟复查。

00:08:44.256 --> 00:08:55.488
Compare leads, position, speed and gain as well as the waveform. A changed electrode position can create an apparent trend that is not a physiological change.
比较波形时也要比导联、体位、速度及增益。电极位置改变可造成并非生理变化的假趋势。

00:08:55.488 --> 00:09:05.592
Report the evolving pattern with the patient response and time. A repeat that looks less dramatic does not independently establish that the danger has resolved.
应按时间交代演变模式及患者反应。复查看起来没那么明显，不能单独证明危险已解除。

00:09:05.592 --> 00:09:19.656
The school uses inferior leads Two, Three and aVF; septal views V one and V two; anterior views V three and V four; and lateral views One, aVL, V five and V six.
学校把II、III、aVF分为下壁，V1、V2为间隔，V3、V4为前壁，I、aVL、V5、V6为侧壁视角。

00:09:19.656 --> 00:09:32.088
These are useful teaching groupings. Anterior and septal regions overlap in clinical interpretation, and the standard lead label does not isolate a perfectly bounded piece of myocardium.
这些是有用教学分组。临床前壁和间隔会重叠，标准导联名称不能隔离边界完美的一小块心肌。

00:09:32.088 --> 00:09:42.576
Contiguous means anatomically related views. Two traces beside each other in the printed layout are not automatically a qualifying anatomical pair.
相邻指解剖相关视角。打印布局中挨在一起的两条，不自动构成符合标准的解剖相邻组合。

00:09:42.576 --> 00:09:53.736
Inspect all leads rather than only the region you expect from the symptom story. A prior infarction or a familiar machine phrase can bias attention away from a new pattern.
应查所有导联，不能只看根据症状预想的区域。既往梗死或熟悉机器短语，可能让你忽视新模式。

00:09:53.736 --> 00:10:05.952
The common teaching associations are inferior with right coronary supply, anterior/septal with the left anterior descending artery and lateral with circumflex-related supply.
常见教学联系是：下壁与右冠供血，前壁间隔与左前降支，侧壁与回旋支相关供血。

00:10:05.952 --> 00:10:18.312
Coronary dominance, branching and overlap vary. Inferior changes are not proof that the right coronary artery is the culprit, and lateral supply is not identical in every person.
冠脉优势型、分支和重叠会变化。下壁变化不能证明责任血管必为右冠，侧壁供血也不是人人相同。

00:10:18.312 --> 00:10:30.624
Localization helps anticipate complications such as conduction disturbance, pump failure or right ventricular involvement, but it is a risk-oriented inference, not definitive anatomy.
定位有助预想传导异常、泵衰竭或右室受累等并发症，但属于风险推断，不是确证解剖。

00:10:30.624 --> 00:10:40.752
Communicate the exact leads and clinical state. That is more defensible than declaring a complete vessel occlusion or a specific lesion from a teaching map alone.
应沟通确切导联和临床状态，这比仅凭教学图宣布完全血管闭塞或特定病灶更有依据。

00:10:40.752 --> 00:10:51.408
Locate QRS end before describing the ST segment. The J point is the boundary between the end of ventricular depolarization and the following segment.
描述ST前先找QRS终点。J点是心室除极结束与随后段落的界限。

00:10:51.408 --> 00:11:03.840
Use a reliable reference and the actual calibration. Baseline wander, a wide QRS, pacing or other repolarization changes can make a simple displacement measurement misleading.
须使用可靠参考及真实校准。基线漂移、宽QRS、起搏或其他复极变化，可能使简单位移测量误导。

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:16.176
The original figure illustrates a baseline segment, elevation and depression at the same represented scale. A single illustrated change is not a full STEMI diagnostic example.
原创图以相同比例示基线、抬高和压低。一个图示变化，不是完整STEMI诊断例。

00:11:16.176 --> 00:11:26.400
Describe what you measured and where. Do not equate every raised segment with infarction or every inverted T with completed irreversible damage.
应说测了什么、在哪里测。不能所有抬高都等于梗死，也不能所有T倒置都等于已完成不可逆损伤。

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:40.104
For the usual adult reference criteria, new J-point ST elevation is assessed in at least two contiguous leads. The general threshold is one millimetre, with a specific exception for V two and V three.
通常成人参考标准在至少两个相邻导联评新发J点ST抬高。一般阈值为一毫米，V2、V3有特定例外。

00:11:40.104 --> 00:11:50.232
In V two and V three the cited thresholds are two point five millimetres for men under forty, two for men forty or older and one point five for women.
V2、V3所引阈值：男性未满40岁为2.5毫米，男性40岁及以上为2毫米，女性为1.5毫米。

00:11:50.232 --> 00:12:04.488
These are qualified reference criteria, not a rule to apply indiscriminately with bundle-branch block, ventricular pacing or marked hypertrophy. Other ischemic patterns may be dangerous without satisfying this table.
这是有条件参考，不能不加区别套于束支阻滞、心室起搏或明显肥厚。其他缺血模式未满足表格，也可能危险。

00:12:04.488 --> 00:12:18.480
Learn the measurements for the school interpretation task, but use the actual PCP acquisition, flagging and consultation pathway operationally. Manual recognition does not create independent reperfusion authority.
学校判图任务要学会测量，但运行中应走实际PCP采集、标记及咨询路径。手动识别不会授予独立再灌注权限。

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:32.136
In original example A, One point five millimetres in Two and aVF exceeds the general one-millimetre reference in an inferior pair, assuming valid acquisition and the required clinical conditions.
原创A例中II、aVF各抬高1.5毫米；假设采集合格且满足临床条件，就超过下壁相邻组合的一般一毫米参考。

00:12:32.136 --> 00:12:45.888
Example B exceeds the cited one point five millimetre V two/V three threshold for women. Example C does not meet the two point five millimetre exception for men under forty.
B例超过女性V2、V3所引1.5毫米阈值；C例未达到未满40岁男性2.5毫米例外阈值。

00:12:45.888 --> 00:12:56.904
Not meeting that numeric table is not a safe rule-out. Symptoms, other leads, reciprocal findings, evolution, equivalents and confounding conduction patterns still matter.
不满足数字表，不是安全排除依据。症状、其他导联、镜像变化、演变、等同表现及传导干扰仍然重要。

00:12:56.904 --> 00:13:08.712
None of these isolated numbers proves the artery, extent or current viability of myocardium. Describe concern and follow the appropriate clinical review and workflow.
这些孤立数字都不能证明责任血管、范围或当前心肌存活性。应描述疑虑并遵适当复核及流程。

00:13:08.712 --> 00:13:21.168
The school describes ischemia, injury and infarction with T-wave, ST and Q-wave changes. Use this to understand possible evolution, not as a mandatory timeline.
学校用T、ST及Q波变化解释缺血、损伤和梗死。应把它理解为可能的演变，而不是必经时间线。

00:13:21.168 --> 00:13:32.664
An acute event may lack a textbook sequence; Q waves can be old, absent or affected by other factors. Waiting for Q waves can delay time-sensitive care.
急性事件未必按教材顺序发展；Q波可为旧有、缺失或受其他因素影响。等Q波出现，可能延误时效治疗。

00:13:32.664 --> 00:13:44.472
A Q wave does not alone confirm that all affected tissue is irreversibly dead, and ST elevation does not prove full-thickness necrosis or complete occlusion in every case.
Q波不能单独确认相关组织全部不可逆坏死；ST抬高也不能在每例都证明透壁坏死或完全闭塞。

00:13:44.472 --> 00:13:56.400
Integrate symptoms, serial ECGs, specialist review and hospital testing. In the field, recognize concern early rather than waiting for a complete diagnostic story.
应综合症状、连续心电、专科复核及医院检查。院前要早识别疑虑，不能等完整诊断故事才行动。

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:05.520
A posterior coronary event may show ST depression in anterior views rather than the obvious standard-lead elevation a beginner expects.
后壁冠脉事件在前方视角可能表现ST压低，而不是初学者预期的标准导联明显抬高。

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:17.016
The school highlights depression and tall R waves in V one to V three as clues. They raise concern in context; they do not diagnose the cause of every anterior depression.
学校强调V1至V3压低及高R作为线索。结合背景时值得担忧，但不能诊断所有前方压低的原因。

00:14:17.016 --> 00:14:31.752
Additional posterior views may help under the actual authorized plan. The current ZOLL procedure labels posterior and right-sided acquisition ACP-only, so this classroom concept does not create an independent PCP procedure.
真实获准方案下，附加后壁导联可能有帮助。当前ZOLL规程把后壁及右胸采集列为ACP专用，课堂概念不会授予PCP独立操作权。

00:14:31.752 --> 00:14:42.480
If electrodes are moved by an authorized clinician, the new designations must be clear. A V seven tracing labelled V four can mislead the receiving team.
获准人员移动电极后，必须明确新名称。V7记录若仍标V4，会误导接收团队。

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:52.608
Left bundle-branch block changes ventricular activation and secondary ST-T appearance. This makes ordinary elevation measurements harder to interpret.
左束支阻滞改变心室激动及继发ST-T外观，使普通抬高测量更难解释。

00:14:52.608 --> 00:15:04.704
The saved school wording calls a new or presumed-new LBBB a STEMI equivalent in context. Current ACS guidance says it is not diagnostic of acute infarction in isolation.
学校存档在相应背景下把新发或疑似新发左束支阻滞称STEMI等同；当前ACS指导指出，单独出现不能诊断急性梗死。

00:15:04.704 --> 00:15:19.008
Symptoms, hemodynamic state, comparison with prior tracings and specialist criteria such as Sgarbossa can change the concern. This is not permission for a beginner to rule in or rule out by one wide complex.
症状、血流动力学、旧图比较及Sgarbossa等专科标准可改变疑虑。不能让初学者凭一个宽波就确诊或排除。

00:15:19.008 --> 00:15:31.296
Treat instability, obtain appropriate support and communicate the exact findings and uncertainty. A normal automated phrase or uncertain onset does not settle the clinical problem.
应处理不稳定、取得支持，并准确沟通所见及不确定性。正常机器短语或起病时间不明，不能解决临床问题。

00:15:31.296 --> 00:15:43.176
Noncoronary and nonacute patterns can produce ST changes, including early repolarization, pericarditis, ventricular hypertrophy and abnormal ventricular activation.
非冠脉及非急性模式也可有ST变化，如早期复极、心包炎、心室肥厚及异常心室激动。

00:15:43.176 --> 00:15:52.488
Technical error can also mimic disease. Confirm correct placement and signal, especially when a pattern conflicts with the clinical picture.
技术错误也可模仿疾病。尤其当图形与患者情况不符时，要确认位置和信号正确。

00:15:52.488 --> 00:16:03.912
Do not rule out coronary disease simply by recognizing one feature associated with a mimic. A person can have a baseline abnormality and a new event together.
不能仅认出一个与模仿情况相关的特征，就排除冠脉病。患者可以同时有基础异常及新发事件。

00:16:03.912 --> 00:16:12.072
Communicate the concern and seek appropriate review rather than creating a confident benign diagnosis from a short classroom checklist.
应沟通疑虑并寻求适当复核，不能凭简短课堂清单，自信宣布良性诊断。

00:16:12.072 --> 00:16:25.488
A normal or nondiagnostic ECG does not exclude acute coronary syndrome. NSTEMI can have nonspecific or absent ECG changes and requires the broader clinical and hospital assessment.
正常或无诊断性心电，不能排除急性冠脉综合征。NSTEMI可能只有非特异变化或完全无变化，需要更全面临床及医院评估。

00:16:25.488 --> 00:16:37.920
Dangerous pulmonary, vascular and other conditions can also occur with a normal tracing. Do not cancel supportive care, transport or escalation solely because the machine says normal.
危险肺部、血管及其他疾病，也可能有正常心电。不能仅因机器说正常，就取消支持、转运或升级。

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:49.752
A person without chest pain can still have an acute coronary presentation. Consider the actual symptom pattern, including breathlessness, weakness, nausea or syncope.
没有胸痛也可能是急性冠脉表现。应结合真实症状模式，包括气促、无力、恶心或晕厥。

00:16:49.752 --> 00:17:00.264
Repeat assessment and obtain indicated review. Improvement of one symptom or one less dramatic tracing does not independently prove safety.
要反复评估并取得有指征复核。一个症状改善，或一次图形不那么明显，不能单独证明安全。

00:17:00.264 --> 00:17:12.768
The school requires verbalizing what else could this be before the first intervention. The purpose is to prevent anchoring, not to demand that every alternative be definitively excluded before help begins.
学校要求首个干预前口述还可能是什么，目的在防锚定，不是要求先把所有替代病因完全排除才开始帮助。

00:17:12.768 --> 00:17:24.648
For chest pressure, important alternatives may include aortic disease, pulmonary embolism or pneumothorax as well as other causes. State a relevant cue that would change the plan.
胸压的重要替代包括主动脉病、肺栓塞、气胸等。应说出能改变方案的相关线索。

00:17:24.648 --> 00:17:36.984
A focused cognitive check can run alongside oxygenation, ventilation and circulation support. It must never become a reason to delay CPR or other immediately indicated care.
简短认知检查可与氧合、通气和循环支持并行，但绝不能成为延误CPR或其他即时有指征照护的理由。

00:17:36.984 --> 00:17:48.432
After each action, ask what changed, what should have changed and whether anything worsened. A new finding should reopen the working explanation instead of being ignored.
每次行动后问什么变了、应怎样变、是否更糟。新发现应重新开启工作解释，而不是被忽略。

00:17:48.432 --> 00:17:58.632
Recognizing a concerning trace is not the end of assessment. Continue support and confirm whether the planned medicine or procedure is appropriate for this patient now.
识别可疑图形不是评估终点。应继续支持，并确认拟用药物或操作此刻适合这位患者。

00:17:58.632 --> 00:18:15.024
Use actual local indications and safeguards for antiplatelet and vasodilator treatment. Hypotension, possible right ventricular involvement and interacting medicines can matter; an ECG label alone is not a nitroglycerin instruction.
抗血小板及扩血管治疗应遵真实本地适应证和保护措施。低血压、可能右室受累及相互作用药物都重要，心电标签不是硝酸甘油指令。

00:18:15.024 --> 00:18:27.768
Oxygen follows the applicable clinical target and exceptions, not a routine response to every chest-pain call. Do not silently replace the current A seven wording with a school blanket range.
给氧应遵相应临床目标及例外，不是每个胸痛都自动给。不能悄悄用学校通用区间替换当前A07。

00:18:27.768 --> 00:18:37.920
Plan rapid appropriate conveyance and early communication. An IV attempt or a desire for a prettier printout must not create an avoidable delay.
应计划快速适当转运并及早沟通。IV尝试或追求更漂亮图形，不能造成可避免延误。

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:50.880
The current public PCP workflow uses a STEMI flag to direct the local pathway, transmission and notification. Request the appropriate support without delaying on scene simply to wait for an intercept.
当前公开PCP流程用STEMI标记指向本地路径、传输和通知。应请求适当支持，但不能只为等会合就在现场拖延。

00:18:50.880 --> 00:19:06.576
An ACUTE MI flag without STEMI does not automatically activate that PCP pathway. The workflow calls for clinical consultation, appropriate support and repeat twelve-leads every ten minutes, with immediate reassessment for deterioration.
只有ACUTE MI、没有STEMI标记，不自动启动该PCP路径。流程要求临床咨询、适当支持及每十分钟复查12导联，恶化时立即重评。

00:19:06.576 --> 00:19:17.832
These are operational distinctions, not a claim that automated software proves or excludes infarction. Follow your actual monitor training and applicable local requirements.
这些是运行区别，不是声称自动软件能证明或排除梗死。应遵实际监护仪训练及适用本地要求。

00:19:17.832 --> 00:19:28.992
Return to the proper monitoring screen after acquisition and document the chosen route of communication. Do not invent a universal destination from a regional pathway used elsewhere.
采集后应回正确监护屏，并记录沟通方式。不能把其他地区路径自创成普遍适用目的地。

00:19:28.992 --> 00:19:38.736
Use the appropriate handover or consultation structure. State your role, the patient's presentation and the time of symptom onset and acquisition.
应采用适当交接或咨询结构，说明身份、患者表现、症状起始及采集时间。

00:19:38.736 --> 00:19:51.312
Describe exact lead findings, the machine flag and any signal limitation. Separate observation from inference, such as inferior elevation rather than certainty about a particular artery.
准确描述导联所见、机器标记及信号限制。把观察与推断分开，例如说下壁抬高，而不是确定某条动脉。

00:19:51.312 --> 00:20:03.864
Include blood pressure and pulse trends, awareness, symptoms, important alternatives and the response to care. Say if a repeat has changed and whether the tracing was actually transmitted.
要含血压脉搏趋势、意识、症状、重要替代解释及照护反应，说明复查是否改变、图形是否真正传出。

00:20:03.864 --> 00:20:16.368
Finish with the intended destination or advice request, estimated arrival and closed-loop confirmation. A clear uncertainty statement is safer than an unsupported confident label.
最后明确目的地或咨询请求、预计到达及闭环确认。清楚说明不确定，比无依据自信标签更安全。

00:20:16.368 --> 00:20:26.208
This is an original teaching case, not the school Wednesday patient. A fifty-eight-year-old has new pressure and nausea with a history of infarction.
这是原创教学案例，不是学校周三患者：58岁，既往梗死，现新发胸压及恶心。

00:20:26.208 --> 00:20:36.936
Obtain appropriate primary assessment and a quality tracing, while the team considers alternatives. Prior infarction does not prove every current change is old.
团队考虑替代解释的同时，应完成适当初评和高质量记录。既往梗死不能证明当前所有变化都是旧的。

00:20:36.936 --> 00:20:48.936
The new inferior pattern and falling pressure demand attention to perfusion and possible complications. Do not give a vasodilator automatically because the complaint is chest pain.
新下壁模式及血压下降，要求关注灌注和可能并发症。不能只因主诉胸痛就自动给扩血管药。

00:20:48.936 --> 00:21:03.864
Follow the actual flag/local pathway, obtain support, communicate the lead findings and hypotension, and reassess after care. Do not delay conveyance to finish a perfect culprit-artery explanation.
应走真实标记及本地路径，求支持，沟通导联所见和低血压，并在照护后复评。不能为完美解释责任动脉而延误转运。

00:21:03.864 --> 00:21:15.840
The saved Seven G lesson asks learners to interpret a series of twelve-lead strips and submit findings. The actual assessed strip set and current submission settings are not recovered here.
7G存档要求学习者判读一组12导联并提交所见。这里尚未取得真实考核图组及当前提交设置。

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:27.216
Use an original practice sheet to organize your own observations: quality and settings, rhythm features, regional changes, clinical context and appropriate next steps.
可用原创练习表组织自己的观察：质量及设置、节律特征、区域变化、临床背景和适当下一步。

00:21:27.216 --> 00:21:38.784
Distinguish what is visible from what cannot be known without symptoms, prior traces or further assessment. Do not present a synthetic example as the answer to a missing assessed strip.
应区分图中可见，与缺少症状、旧图或进一步评估就无法知道的事。不能把合成例子冒充缺失考核图的答案。

00:21:38.784 --> 00:21:47.592
This course can teach and provide practice; it does not submit work, open a quiz or certify the school assignment as completed.
本课程可以教授并提供练习，但不会提交作业、打开测验，或认证学校任务已完成。

00:21:47.592 --> 00:21:57.528
Point to each anatomical landmark on the training model and explain why V four precedes V three and why V five and V six stay level.
在训练模型上指出每个解剖标志，解释为什么先V4后V3，以及为什么V5、V6保持水平。

00:21:57.528 --> 00:22:06.024
Rehearse the under-three-minute school target with a partner, measuring actual quality and time rather than treating speed alone as success.
与同伴演练学校三分钟内目标，同时测真实质量和时间，不能把速度单独当成功。

00:22:06.024 --> 00:22:16.584
Explain the V two/V three threshold exception, why new LBBB is not an isolated diagnosis and why a normal tracing cannot rule out ACS.
解释V2、V3阈值例外、新发左束支阻滞为何不能单独诊断，以及正常图为何不能排除ACS。

00:22:16.584 --> 00:22:26.400
Finish with a concise report and the school reassessment questions. The important endpoint is a safer care sequence, not a memorized vessel label.
最后完成简洁报告及学校复评问题。重要终点是更安全的照护顺序，不是背下某个血管标签。
